Hi Brian,

I hope you are having a good break. I=92m checking in now, but feel free to=
 wait to reply here. I=92ve drafted a statement of Stakeholders and researc=
h questions, pasted below. I=92d love some feedback - I don=92t want to mis=
understand or steer our team without deliberation. The questions were more =
just from what I could think of, not what I think we necessarily need to do=
.

Let me know whenever you get around to it.

Best,
Matt


The primary stakeholders:

Daniel F. Bassil, (the sponsor and head of Tutor/Mentor Institute) who want=
 to track the people who attend events, and what their role is in relation =
to mentorship. For example, could be a current volunteer/volunteer, a poten=
tial volunteer/mentor, a director or other worker at a non-profit, an indep=
endent community organizer, etc.

Non-profit leaders and staff related to or aligned with the Tutor/Mentor In=
stitute who may be interested in learning from and replicating his methodol=
ogy in trying to tackle poverty through mentorship. The visitor may want to=
 get a sense of the types of people who are currently attending events, or =
they may want specific information about individuals that they may wish to =
contact.

Participants in Tutor/Mentor Institute events who may wish to track their p=
articipation and connections to other attendees/volunteers. These stakehold=
ers may wish to see their own network and to find people or roles in their =
network=92s network.

Potentially, researchers who want to understand the methodology. They will =
likely be less interested in the specifics than in the structure and what i=
s learned from this type of analysis.



Research Questions include: How to effectively organize the network to be u=
seful to a user who does not know any specific people (nodes)?

Can we show a time progression here to demonstrate how this network forms a=
nd expands?

Can we correlate these networks to any results? Have these networks been sh=
own to be effective in addressing poverty?

Are there any highly active or influential nodes or =93supernodes=94 (aside=
 from Daniel)? How influential are they at connecting people and ideas?



--

